+### [GPU-based Tiled Ray Casting with Depth Peeling](9631-gpu-based-tiled-ray-casting-with-depth-peeling.md)
+This method is a hardware-accelerated ray casting algorithm for volume rendering of time-varying scalar fields on unstructured tetrahedral meshes. It solves the problem of rendering non-convex meshes on GPUs by combining screen tiling for performance with depth peeling to correctly handle ray re-entry into the mesh. It sets itself apart from its sibling [Hardware-Accelerated Volume Rendering](5616-hardware-accelerated-volume-rendering.md) by explicitly addressing non-convexity without convexification, and from [WebGL Path Tracing Volume Rendering](8592-webgl-path-tracing-volume-rendering.md) by using deterministic ray casting on unstructured grids rather than path tracing on regular grids.
